===== path p track
Incrementally build a Toolpath Path document

Usage: path p track [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  init      Start a tracking session; reads initial content from stdin
  step      Record a new step; reads current content from stdin
  visit     Cache content at a sequence number without creating a step; reads content from stdin. Used when navigating history (undo/redo)
  note      Set intent on the current head step
  annotate  Set metadata on a step (intent, source, refs)
  export    Emit the session as a Toolpath Path document
  close     Export and delete the session state file
  list      List active tracking sessions
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --pretty
          Pretty-print JSON output

      --picker <PICKER>
          Backend for the interactive fuzzy picker used by `share`, `resume`, and `p import <provider>`. `auto` (default) uses the embedded skim picker and falls back to external `fzf` only when skim isn't compiled in; a hint is printed if `fzf` is also on PATH. `fzf`/`skim` force one backend and error if it isn't available

          Possible values:
          - auto: Pick whichever backend is available; prefer the embedded skim picker and fall back to external `fzf` when skim isn't compiled in. When external `fzf` is also on `PATH`, a one-time hint is printed to stderr advising `--picker fzf` for users who want their fzf config / keybindings
          - fzf:  Force the external `fzf` binary. Errors if it isn't on `PATH`
          - skim: Force the embedded skim picker. Errors if path-cli was built with `--no-default-features`
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
===== path p track annotate
Set metadata on a step (intent, source, refs)

Usage: path p track annotate [OPTIONS] --session <SESSION>

Options:
      --session <SESSION>
          Path to session state file

      --step <STEP>
          Step ID to annotate (defaults to head)

      --intent <INTENT>
          Intent text

      --source <SOURCE>
          VCS source as JSON (e.g. '{"type":"git","revision":"abc123"}')

      --ref <REFS>
          Reference as JSON (e.g. '{"rel":"issue","href":"https://..."}'), repeatable

      --pretty
          Pretty-print JSON output

      --picker <PICKER>
          Backend for the interactive fuzzy picker used by `share`, `resume`, and `p import <provider>`. `auto` (default) uses the embedded skim picker and falls back to external `fzf` only when skim isn't compiled in; a hint is printed if `fzf` is also on PATH. `fzf`/`skim` force one backend and error if it isn't available

          Possible values:
          - auto: Pick whichever backend is available; prefer the embedded skim picker and fall back to external `fzf` when skim isn't compiled in. When external `fzf` is also on `PATH`, a one-time hint is printed to stderr advising `--picker fzf` for users who want their fzf config / keybindings
          - fzf:  Force the external `fzf` binary. Errors if it isn't on `PATH`
          - skim: Force the embedded skim picker. Errors if path-cli was built with `--no-default-features`
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
