===== path p track visit
Cache content at a sequence number without creating a step; reads content from stdin. Used when navigating history (undo/redo)

Usage: path p track visit [OPTIONS] --session <SESSION> --seq <SEQ>

Options:
      --session <SESSION>
          Path to session state file

      --seq <SEQ>
          Sequence number to cache

      --inherit-from <INHERIT_FROM>
          Inherit seq_to_step mapping from this ancestor seq

      --pretty
          Pretty-print JSON output

      --picker <PICKER>
          Backend for the interactive fuzzy picker used by `share`, `resume`, and `p import <provider>`. `auto` (default) uses the embedded skim picker and falls back to external `fzf` only when skim isn't compiled in; a hint is printed if `fzf` is also on PATH. `fzf`/`skim` force one backend and error if it isn't available

